1
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:46,000
The fight was against the raiders... but the feud was between themselves!

2
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:26,000
Buck and the Preacher is a action, comedy, western
film directed by Sidney Poitier.

3
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:06,000
A wagon master and a con-man preacher help freed slaves
dogged by cheap-labor agents out West.

4
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:46,000
Buck, played by Sidney Poitier.

5
00:28:20,000 --> 00:28:26,000
Preacher, played by Harry Belafonte.

6
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:06,000
Ruth, played by Ruby Dee.

7
00:39:40,000 --> 00:39:46,000
Deshay, played by Cameron Mitchell.

8
00:45:20,000 --> 00:45:26,000
Floyd, played by Denny Miller.

9
00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:06,000
Madam Esther, played by Nita Talbot.

10
00:56:40,000 --> 00:56:46,000
Buck and the Preacher is a 1972 American Western film released by Columbia
Pictures, written by Ernest Kinoy and directed by Sidney Poitier.

11
01:02:20,000 --> 01:02:26,000
Poitier also stars in the film alongside Harry Belafonte and Ruby Dee.

12
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
This is the first film Sidney Poitier directed.

13
01:13:40,000 --> 01:13:46,000
Vincent Canby of The New York Times said Poitier "showed a talent for easy,
unguarded, rambunctious humor missing from his more stately movies".

14
01:19:20,000 --> 01:19:26,000
This film broke Hollywood Western traditions by casting black actors as central characters and portraying both
tension and solidarity between African Americans and Native Americans in the late 19th century.

15
01:25:00,000 --> 01:25:06,000
The notable blues musicians Sonny Terry, Brownie McGhee, and Don Frank Brooks
performed in the film's soundtrack, composed by jazz great Benny Carter.

16
01:30:40,000 --> 01:30:46,000
The film explores themes of con man, kansas, usa, preacher, wagon master, 1860s.

17
01:36:20,000 --> 01:36:26,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
